From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:29:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: correct the comment on unmaps of unregistered DMA
 ranges

The comment quotes a gpu_vaspace.c assertion, "0 == (pMapNode->gpuMask &
gpuMask)", that does not exist in this driver release; a map at a VA that
is still mapped fails the "range must not already be mapped" check in
_gvaspaceMappingInsert() instead. It also names the automatic unmap of
back references as the case the no-op is for, but that path passes a size
of 0, for which the resource server drops its inter-mapping whether the
unmap fails or not. A stale inter-mapping is only kept for an unmap with
an explicit size, which the resource server re-adds on failure.

Describe the remaining no-op case as it is now that a request covering a
later DMA mapping unmaps that mapping, and say that each occurrence is a
mismatch to look into.

Fixes: 0eb096761eee ("nvidia: treat an unmap of an unregistered DMA mapping range as a no-op")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c | 18 ++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
index ab5ff400..7e34bbd5 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/virtual_mem.c
@@ -1802,14 +1802,16 @@ virtmemUnmapFrom_IMPL
             // Nothing is registered for this range any more.
             //
             // This happens when an earlier partial unmap already released
-            // all pages of the request, or when inter-mapping registration
-            // failed after the client mapping had been torn down.  Treat the
-            // unmap as a no-op so that cleanup paths (notably the automatic
-            // unmapping of back references in rs_client.c) can retire their
-            // own bookkeeping instead of failing and leaving stale
-            // inter-mapping nodes behind, which later surface as "Duplicate
-            // inter mapping" / "0 == (pMapNode->gpuMask & gpuMask)" failures
-            // on unrelated mappings.
+            // all mapping pages of the request, or when inter-mapping
+            // registration failed after the client mapping had been torn
+            // down.  Treat the unmap as a no-op so that the resource server
+            // can retire its own inter-mapping instead of keeping a stale
+            // node, which a later map at the same dmaOffset would collide
+            // with ("Duplicate inter mapping detected").
+            //
+            // Apart from server fragments that a partial unmap above left
+            // entirely in released pages, each occurrence means the two
+            // lists disagreed; it is logged and counted, not handled.
             //
             if (pVirtualMemory->orphanedServerFragments > 0)
             {
